1
00:00:00,261 --> 00:00:01,946
Last video ended on this question:

2
00:00:02,609 --> 00:00:04,695
if a curve has gradient two x at

3
00:00:04,796 --> 00:00:05,317
every x,

4
00:00:05,919 --> 00:00:06,561
which curve is it?

5
00:00:07,385 --> 00:00:08,931
Here's that rule on a plant stand.

6
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:11,884
Three bean plants grow by the same rule.

7
00:00:12,547 --> 00:00:15,412
t weeks after they sprout, each tip rises

8
00:00:15,574 --> 00:00:17,417
at two t centimetres per week.

9
00:00:18,141 --> 00:00:20,727
So each tip's height has gradient two t

10
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:21,669
at every moment.

11
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:24,356
But they sit on different shelves, so their

12
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:25,820
height graphs are the same shape,

13
00:00:26,322 --> 00:00:26,662
slid up.

14
00:00:27,586 --> 00:00:28,406
Now one fact:

15
00:00:29,089 --> 00:00:31,613
one tip is sixty-six centimetres above the floor

16
00:00:31,755 --> 00:00:32,555
after four weeks.

17
00:00:33,398 --> 00:00:34,266
Which shelf is it on?

18
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,915
And how does a whole family of curves

19
00:00:36,976 --> 00:00:38,018
become one curve?

20
00:00:38,711 --> 00:00:40,085
Here's the name for what we're finding.

21
00:00:40,709 --> 00:00:43,374
If a function, capital F, has derivative f,

22
00:00:43,876 --> 00:00:46,201
then capital F is called a primitive of

23
00:00:46,222 --> 00:00:46,261
f.

24
00:00:47,344 --> 00:00:49,368
So x squared is a primitive of two

25
00:00:49,529 --> 00:00:49,648
x,

26
00:00:50,291 --> 00:00:52,254
and each tip's height is a primitive of

27
00:00:52,315 --> 00:00:52,976
its growth rate.

28
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:56,388
Finding a primitive runs differentiation backwards.

29
00:00:57,112 --> 00:00:59,560
Differentiating takes x squared to two x.

30
00:01:00,164 --> 00:01:02,214
Finding a primitive starts at two x and

31
00:01:02,376 --> 00:01:02,596
asks,

32
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:04,044
what did this come from?

33
00:01:04,696 --> 00:01:06,061
Why do so many curves fit?

34
00:01:06,946 --> 00:01:09,318
Adding a constant slides a curve straight up

35
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,289
or down, without tilting it anywhere.

36
00:01:11,911 --> 00:01:14,236
At every x, the slid curve has the

37
00:01:14,297 --> 00:01:17,102
same gradient as x squared, because the derivative

38
00:01:17,143 --> 00:01:18,185
of a constant is zero.

39
00:01:18,969 --> 00:01:20,675
So if capital F is one primitive,

40
00:01:21,259 --> 00:01:23,487
F plus any constant is also a primitive.

41
00:01:24,171 --> 00:01:25,960
We write the constant as C, and the

42
00:01:26,001 --> 00:01:27,971
family as F of x, plus C.

43
00:01:28,408 --> 00:01:30,536
But could a curve that isn't a slid

44
00:01:30,577 --> 00:01:32,665
copy also have gradient two x?

45
00:01:33,529 --> 00:01:35,921
Take any two primitives of the same function,

46
00:01:36,303 --> 00:01:37,569
and look at the gap between them.

47
00:01:38,313 --> 00:01:40,137
For two of the shoots, it stays thirty

48
00:01:40,179 --> 00:01:41,381
centimetres all the way up.

49
00:01:42,105 --> 00:01:44,956
Their gradients are equal at every x, so

50
00:01:45,117 --> 00:01:47,205
the gap's gradient is zero everywhere.

51
00:01:48,089 --> 00:01:50,835
A function whose gradient is zero everywhere never

52
00:01:50,916 --> 00:01:52,358
rises and never falls.

53
00:01:53,061 --> 00:01:56,320
So over an unbroken interval, it stays constant.

54
00:01:57,064 --> 00:01:59,572
That means any two primitives differ by a

55
00:01:59,653 --> 00:02:00,074
constant,

56
00:02:00,596 --> 00:02:02,963
and F of x, plus C, covers every

57
00:02:03,065 --> 00:02:03,405
one of them.

58
00:02:04,008 --> 00:02:06,135
So how do we find one primitive?

59
00:02:06,863 --> 00:02:07,836
Reverse the power rule.

60
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:11,247
Differentiating multiplies by the power, then lowers it

61
00:02:11,288 --> 00:02:11,668
by one.

62
00:02:12,331 --> 00:02:12,913
To undo it,

63
00:02:13,456 --> 00:02:15,846
raise the power by one, then divide by

64
00:02:15,888 --> 00:02:16,670
the new power.

65
00:02:17,515 --> 00:02:18,459
Try x squared.

66
00:02:19,164 --> 00:02:21,112
Raising the power gives x cubed.

67
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:24,687
But x cubed differentiates to three x squared,

68
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:26,013
three times too big.

69
00:02:26,778 --> 00:02:27,745
So divide by three.

70
00:02:28,509 --> 00:02:31,556
x cubed over three differentiates to x squared.

71
00:02:32,282 --> 00:02:33,011
Watch its gradient.

72
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,184
At every x, the gradient of x cubed

73
00:02:36,205 --> 00:02:38,949
over three equals the height of x squared.

74
00:02:39,833 --> 00:02:41,979
In general, x to the n plus one,

75
00:02:42,321 --> 00:02:44,949
over n plus one, differentiates to x to

76
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:45,290
the n.

77
00:02:46,014 --> 00:02:47,927
The n plus one cancels, as long as

78
00:02:47,968 --> 00:02:48,551
it isn't zero.

79
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:51,299
So for x above zero, it works for

80
00:02:51,541 --> 00:02:53,825
every real n except minus one.

81
00:02:54,489 --> 00:02:56,685
Two more facts handle whole polynomials.

82
00:02:57,169 --> 00:02:59,120
The derivative of a sum is the sum

83
00:02:59,242 --> 00:03:00,006
of the derivatives.

84
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:02,412
So if F is a primitive of f,

85
00:03:02,814 --> 00:03:05,057
and G is a primitive of g, then

86
00:03:05,338 --> 00:03:07,321
F plus G is a primitive of f

87
00:03:07,402 --> 00:03:07,741
plus g.

88
00:03:08,585 --> 00:03:10,973
And k times F is a primitive of

89
00:03:11,054 --> 00:03:13,542
k times f, for any constant k.

90
00:03:14,507 --> 00:03:16,255
Now the notation for the whole family.

91
00:03:16,899 --> 00:03:19,027
The integral of f of x, d x,

92
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:20,996
equals F of x, plus C.

93
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:24,425
The function inside is called the integrand, and

94
00:03:24,566 --> 00:03:26,630
d x says that x is the variable.

95
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:29,805
This is called the indefinite integral, and finding

96
00:03:29,846 --> 00:03:30,991
it is called integration.

97
00:03:31,755 --> 00:03:33,377
So the integral of x to the n

98
00:03:33,819 --> 00:03:35,962
is x to the n plus one, over

99
00:03:36,144 --> 00:03:37,385
n plus one, plus C.

100
00:03:38,216 --> 00:03:39,463
Now a worked example.

101
00:03:40,207 --> 00:03:43,437
Find the integral of three x squared, plus

102
00:03:43,498 --> 00:03:46,045
four x, minus five, d x.

103
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:47,861
Work term by term.

104
00:03:48,568 --> 00:03:52,240
Three x squared becomes three, times x cubed

105
00:03:52,361 --> 00:03:52,882
over three,

106
00:03:53,385 --> 00:03:54,387
which is x cubed.

107
00:03:55,271 --> 00:03:57,577
Four x is four x to the one,

108
00:03:57,999 --> 00:04:00,746
so it becomes four, times x squared over

109
00:04:00,827 --> 00:04:01,087
two,

110
00:04:01,690 --> 00:04:02,792
which is two x squared.

111
00:04:03,676 --> 00:04:06,183
Minus five is minus five x to the

112
00:04:06,245 --> 00:04:08,833
zero, so it becomes minus five x.

113
00:04:09,897 --> 00:04:12,541
Add one C for the whole answer, because

114
00:04:12,583 --> 00:04:15,046
the constants from each term combine into a

115
00:04:15,168 --> 00:04:15,968
single constant.

116
00:04:16,672 --> 00:04:18,318
Now check by differentiating back.

117
00:04:19,001 --> 00:04:21,927
The derivative is three x squared, plus four

118
00:04:22,029 --> 00:04:23,331
x, minus five.

119
00:04:23,995 --> 00:04:25,488
That's the integrand exactly.

120
00:04:26,361 --> 00:04:28,409
Now the main idea in one problem.

121
00:04:29,111 --> 00:04:31,274
A curve has gradient d y by d

122
00:04:31,435 --> 00:04:34,519
x equals three x squared, minus four x,

123
00:04:34,659 --> 00:04:35,260
plus two,

124
00:04:35,761 --> 00:04:38,124
and it passes through the point one, five.

125
00:04:38,866 --> 00:04:39,874
Find its equation.

126
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,604
Integrate first.

127
00:04:42,387 --> 00:04:45,113
y equals x cubed, minus two x squared,

128
00:04:45,454 --> 00:04:47,017
plus two x, plus C.

129
00:04:47,659 --> 00:04:49,787
That's a whole family, every member the same

130
00:04:49,868 --> 00:04:50,128
shape.

131
00:04:50,835 --> 00:04:51,907
The point picks one.

132
00:04:52,533 --> 00:04:55,828
Substitute x equals one, and y equals five.

133
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:59,779
Five equals one, minus two, plus two, plus

134
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,362
C, which is one plus C.

135
00:05:02,646 --> 00:05:03,779
So C is four.

136
00:05:04,526 --> 00:05:07,390
The curve is y equals x cubed, minus

137
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:10,016
two x squared, plus two x, plus four.

138
00:05:10,799 --> 00:05:12,565
A fact like this, the value of the

139
00:05:12,606 --> 00:05:15,196
function at one x, is called an initial

140
00:05:15,237 --> 00:05:15,638
condition.

141
00:05:16,383 --> 00:05:17,390
Back to the plant stand.

142
00:05:17,852 --> 00:05:20,601
Each tip's height is t squared, plus C.

143
00:05:21,464 --> 00:05:23,586
The tip that's sixty-six centimetres up at four

144
00:05:23,666 --> 00:05:27,330
weeks has sixteen, plus C, equals sixty-six,

145
00:05:27,831 --> 00:05:28,952
so C is fifty.

146
00:05:29,593 --> 00:05:31,822
It started at fifty centimetres, on the middle

147
00:05:31,862 --> 00:05:32,103
shelf.

148
00:05:32,931 --> 00:05:34,061
C isn't sixty-six.

149
00:05:34,607 --> 00:05:36,134
Sixty-six is where it got to.

150
00:05:37,079 --> 00:05:38,054
C is where it started.

151
00:05:38,709 --> 00:05:39,654
Here's the idea to keep.

152
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:42,138
The gradient rule fixes the shape.

153
00:05:42,904 --> 00:05:44,329
One point fixes the height.

154
00:05:45,334 --> 00:05:47,459
For the plant stand, the growth rule fixed

155
00:05:47,481 --> 00:05:49,907
the shape, and one reading fixed the shelf.

156
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:53,311
To find the shape, raise the power, divide

157
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:55,354
by the new power, and add C.

158
00:05:55,997 --> 00:05:57,384
Then differentiate back to check.

159
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:00,294
Your turn.

160
00:06:00,998 --> 00:06:04,339
Find the integral of eight x cubed, minus

161
00:06:04,541 --> 00:06:07,201
six x squared, plus five, d x,

162
00:06:07,803 --> 00:06:09,763
and check your answer by differentiating.

163
00:06:10,167 --> 00:06:11,159
Pause here to answer.

164
00:06:22,022 --> 00:06:24,212
Eight x cubed becomes eight x to the

165
00:06:24,292 --> 00:06:26,362
four over four, which is two x to

166
00:06:26,402 --> 00:06:26,724
the four.

167
00:06:27,566 --> 00:06:30,674
Minus six x squared becomes minus two x

168
00:06:30,755 --> 00:06:31,076
cubed.

169
00:06:31,859 --> 00:06:33,052
Five becomes five x.

170
00:06:33,658 --> 00:06:35,502
So the answer is two x to the

171
00:06:35,563 --> 00:06:38,609
four, minus two x cubed, plus five x,

172
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:39,291
plus C.

173
00:06:40,294 --> 00:06:43,521
Differentiating gives eight x cubed, minus six x

174
00:06:43,582 --> 00:06:45,645
squared, plus five, which matches.

175
00:06:46,428 --> 00:06:48,656
Without the C, you'd have just one primitive,

176
00:06:48,898 --> 00:06:49,399
not all of them.

177
00:06:51,114 --> 00:06:51,542
Last one.

178
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:55,111
A curve has gradient function f prime of

179
00:06:55,273 --> 00:06:58,436
x equals four x cubed, minus six x,

180
00:06:58,537 --> 00:06:59,117
plus one,

181
00:06:59,698 --> 00:07:01,940
and it passes through the point two, nine.

182
00:07:02,644 --> 00:07:03,656
Find f of x.

183
00:07:04,447 --> 00:07:05,439
Pause here to answer.

184
00:07:16,379 --> 00:07:17,088
Integrate first.

185
00:07:17,936 --> 00:07:19,559
f of x is x to the four,

186
00:07:20,001 --> 00:07:22,546
minus three x squared, plus x, plus C.

187
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:24,257
Now use the point.

188
00:07:24,979 --> 00:07:28,240
At x equals two, that's sixteen, minus twelve,

189
00:07:28,542 --> 00:07:29,101
plus two,

190
00:07:29,622 --> 00:07:31,463
plus C, which is six plus C.

191
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:34,854
It must equal nine, so C is three.

192
00:07:35,658 --> 00:07:37,040
f of x is x to the four,

193
00:07:37,442 --> 00:07:40,389
minus three x squared, plus x, plus three.

194
00:07:41,112 --> 00:07:43,139
C isn't the y-value, nine.

195
00:07:43,602 --> 00:07:45,832
It's the slide from six up to nine.

196
00:07:47,568 --> 00:07:50,757
So a family of primitives becomes one curve

197
00:07:50,978 --> 00:07:52,542
once a single point is known.

198
00:07:53,766 --> 00:07:56,453
Next, the power is on a bracket: the

199
00:07:56,535 --> 00:07:59,001
integral of two x plus one, all squared.

200
00:07:59,708 --> 00:08:00,803
You could expand it first.

201
00:08:00,865 --> 00:08:02,183
But is there a shortcut?

202
00:08:04,755 --> 00:08:05,638
Here are the key notes.

203
00:08:06,161 --> 00:08:07,929
Pause the video if you need more time

204
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:08,431
to copy them.
